{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ dispose electronic devices recycle donate erase data)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_667205732#2_1555427864","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3593","rank":1,"snippet":"refurbish computers for reuse. The contractor also may recover metals and plastic components from the computers and sell them. The County requires its contractor and non-profit partners to erase data from equipment that will be reused and to destroy remaining memory <cover>devices. While we take reasonable measures to work with reputable companies and organizations, we recommend that you protect against unauthorized use of personal information. Use a data-wiping tool to erase personal data before dropping electronics off for recycling. Examples of “personal information” include Internet browser’s cache, cookies, history email contacts and messages documents recycle bin or trash folder items passwords to cloud services all nontransferable software You can find data-wiping tools online at no cost. Where may I donate working computers and other electronic items? A resource listing of several organizations for reuse opportunities. Check the Montgomery County Volunteer Center's list of local donation opportunities, which includes computers.\" , \"start_char\": 3011.000000 , \"title\": \"Electronics – How to recycle/dispose – </cover>Montgomery County, Maryland\" , \"url\": \"https://www2.montgomerycountymd.gov/DepHowDoI/material.aspx?tag=electronics&material_key=37\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"0/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_667205732#2_1555427864","relevance":3,"reason":"The result is a dedicated county page titled 'Electronics – How to recycle/dispose' and gives direct steps such as using data-wiping tools before recycling and donation options for working electronics.","learned":"Individuals should erase personal data with a data-wiping tool before dropping electronics off for recycling, and may donate working devices to reuse organizations."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3593","reason":"The initial query produced a highly relevant disposal guidance page; continue to find additional grade-3 documents."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3593"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_264600753#1_600078202","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3593","rank":2,"snippet":"drive? Tony Landry \" , \"segment\": \"Don’t throw away laptops because like any other <cover>electronic gadgets, laptops too have some hazardous substances which are very harmful to the environment. Instead user can opt for, re-selling, donating or recycling laptops. Re-Selling: Some people and organization buy used laptops so it is better to resell old laptops instead of throwing them. Donate: There are many organizations that collect old laptops and computers and give them to charities. Recycle: User can give their old laptops to the manufacturer who has some programs to recycles laptop and its components. Above are some ways which you can opt, but before opting you have to take some precautions, because these ways have some limitations with respect to data security. Disposing old laptops or other data storage devices with data in it may invite many threats to the user, so proper method must be carried out to erase data from it.\" , \"start_char\": 527.000000 , \"title\": \"How to Dispose </cover>Laptop Safely - Info | Remo Software\" , \"url\": \"https://www.remosoftware.com/info/how-to-"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"1/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_264600753#1_600078202","relevance":3,"reason":"The page is dedicated to safely disposing of laptops and gives direct steps applicable to electronic devices: do not throw them away, resell, donate, recycle through manufacturer programs, and erase data first.","learned":"Old laptops/electronic gadgets should be resold, donated, or recycled rather than trashed, and users should wipe stored data before disposal."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3593","reason":"This query is returning directly relevant disposal-step documents, so continue through the ranked results for more grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3593"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_667205732#1_1555425188","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3593","rank":3,"snippet":"<cover>recycle / dispose electronics What items are accepted as electronics? What items are not accepted as electronics? May I deliver electronic items with a truck? What happens to my computer and data after recycling drop-off? Where may I donate working computers and other electronic items? I can't bring my electronics to the Transfer Station or Community-Based Drop-off Events. What other eCycling options do I have? Community-based options Locations accepted \" , \"segment\": \"What items are not accepted as electronics? Our electronics recycling program does not accept these items Audiotapes Videotapes However, these items are accepted for recycling through other recycling programs, which you can locate through these resources Earth911 recycling location lookup tool for electronics Electronics Recycling (eCycling) - list maintained by the Maryland Department of the Environment Nationwide donation or recycling options for old computers and other electronic products - list maintained by the US EPA Small household appliances – these items are accepted for recycling as scrap metal. Rechargeable batteries, large or small - take rechargeable batteries to our Household Hazardous Waste drop-off, also located in the Transfer Station's Recycling area - see more about batteries uninterruptible power supplies (personal & network) tool batteries</cover>"}}
