{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1932927485#4_3118383344","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of a dedicated Goodwill page on consciously recycling e-waste. Although the visible segment is mostly e-waste facts, the page is centered on electronics recycling/donation and includes relevant sections such as what can be donated, Goodwill/Dell Reconnect, and personal data notice, directly supporting proper disposal through donation/recycling rather than landfill.","learned":"Goodwill/Dell Reconnect-style programs are disposal options for electronics, and e-waste recycling recovers valuable materials while avoiding toxic landfill waste."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3597","reason":"The current query is still producing authoritative or dedicated electronics recycling/data-security pages, though with some duplicate segments; continue to find any remaining distinct grade-3 results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3597"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_667205732#4_1555432013","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3597","rank":8,"snippet":"to <cover>recycle / dispose electronics What items are accepted as electronics? What items are not accepted as electronics? May I deliver electronic items with a truck? What happens to my computer and data after recycling drop-off? Where may I donate working computers and other electronic items? I can't bring my electronics to the Transfer Station or Community-Based Drop-off Events. What other eCycling options do I have? Community-based options Locations accepted \" , \"segment\": \"Local computer reuse organizations also accept donations of computers and related items. I can't bring my electronics to the Transfer Station or Community-Based Drop-off Events. What other eCycling options do I have? Recycling options for cell phones A variety of organizations offer trade-in, take back or drop-off programs. Some of them provide this service at no cost for to you, some charge you a fee, and others may offer credit towards the purchase of new equipment. Earth911 recycling location lookup tool for electronics Electronics Recycling (eCycling) - list maintained by the Maryland Department of the Environment Nationwide donation or recycling options for old computers and other electronic products - list maintained by the US EPA</cover>Community-"}}
