{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_667205732#4_1555432013","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of the dedicated Montgomery County page on how to recycle/dispose electronics. It directly lists practical options for individuals such as donating computers to reuse organizations, using transfer station or community drop-off events, trade-in/take-back/drop-off programs for phones, Earth911, state eCycling lists, and EPA donation/recycling resources.","learned":"If individuals cannot use a local transfer station or drop-off event, they can use trade-in, take-back, or drop-off programs, Earth911, state eCycling lists, EPA resources, or local reuse organizations for working devices."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3597","reason":"The current query is still returning dedicated and authoritative electronics disposal guidance; continue to retrieve more grade-3 evidence until relevance drops or the list is exhausted."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3597"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1675264766#5_3315060849","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3597","rank":10,"snippet":"<cover>Electronics Before Recycling By Kathryn Sukalich Back Up Your Data Use a Data Erasing Program If You’re Still Concerned, Consider Physical Destruction Recycle or Donate \" , \"segment\": \"Best Buy’s Geek Squad offers a helpful video explaining this process. For Mac users, Apple provides detailed instructions for how to securely erase your data. Instead of using a downloaded program, boot your computer using its installation disc and then use your system’s Disk Utility to do the erasure. For both Macs and PCs, you can select how many times you want to write over the files. The more times you write over your data, the more secure it is, but keep in mind that the time it takes to complete this increases significantly the more times you overwrite. Apple explains that writing over data three times meets the Department of Energy’s standards, and writing over it seven times meets the Department of Defense’s requirements for erasing data. For added security, you can consider encrypting all of your sensitive files before deleting them. According to PC World, a data recovery program could potentially restore a file, but wouldn’t be able to decrypt </cover>","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_667205732#1_1555425188","rank":9,"relevance":3}]}}
{"request":{"judgments":"23/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1675264766#5_3315060849","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of the dedicated Earth911 page on removing data from electronics before recycling. It provides concrete data-preparation steps such as securely erasing Macs/PCs, overwriting files multiple times, and encrypting sensitive files before deletion, as part of the larger recycle-or-donate process.","learned":"Before recycling or donating computers, individuals can securely erase data using system tools or erasure programs, overwrite data for stronger protection, and encrypt sensitive files before deletion."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3597","reason":"The EPA-oriented query remains productive for direct electronics recycling and data-security guidance; continue to see if additional distinct grade-3 results remain."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3597"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1377579587#2_2864435394","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3597","rank":11,"snippet":"in for cold, hard cash. If you want to sell it yourself, head to Craigslist, Amazon or eBay. For hassle-free trade-ins, use Gazelle. Donate your old devices to a cause you care about. If it’s broken or just too old to sell or <cover>donate, dispose of it safely. Don’t forget to cancel unnecessary subscriptions. Bonus Tip: Back up your data, then delete everything. Don’t those old electronics get dusty in your junk drawer – recycle them! Why not make some money while doing your part to make the world a better place? \" , \"segment\": \"Just bring them in, and you’ll get a quote that you can put toward the purchase of something new at GameStop, put on a gift card, or carry out in cash. For other options to trade items back to the original manufacturer, check out this list provided by the EPA. </cover>If you want to sell it yourself, head to Craigslist, Amazon or eBay. If your device is still in good working order and you want to get a nice chunk of change out of it, your best bet is to sell it on Craigslist , Amazon or "}}
