{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"how to recycle old electronics\" erase data donate)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_1409165127#3_2925404489","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3601","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_1409165127#3_2925404489\" , \"end_char\": 2675.000000 , \"headings\": \"How to Recycle Old Electronics<cover>How to Recycle Old Electronics 3 smart, responsible tactics for getting rid of unwanted laptops, phones, and more 1. Take It to a Recycler 2. Donate It 3. Take It to a Tech Firm How do you recycle your old electronics? 5 Things to Always Recycle 150 \" , \"segment\": \"But no matter where you live, there are safe methods for disposal. First, make sure to completely erase all personal information. It usually isn’t as simple as deleting files. Here's how to get your personal data </cover>off a laptop, for example. Once that's done, here are your options. 1. Take It to a Recycler Plenty of nonprofit organizations and local communities offer options to help you recycle old electronics. One group, Call2Recycle, offers drop-off locations for rechargeable batteries and cell phones all over the U.S. To find a location, just enter your ZIP code at Call2Recycle.org. Access may be limited due to concerns about "}}
