{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3604"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_861229317#3_1956786279","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3604","rank":4,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_861229317#3_1956786279\" , \"end_char\": 2055.000000 , \"headings\": \"How to Dispose of Old Computers and Other Company Hardware How to Dispose of Old Computers and Other Company Hardware You’re ready to <cover>get rid of some old equipment. How can you do that safely? 1. Backup your data. 2. Wipe your hard drive. 3. Donate, resell, or recycle. Consult with a professional about regulatory standards. \" , \"segment\": \"Wipe your hard drive. Clearing data off our computer </cover>is no easy process. To ensure that no sensitive company of customer data can be recovered by data thieves, follow this multi-step process. Delete all your files. You may have heard how hard it is to permanently delete data from your hard drive. Simply emptying your recycling bin isn’t enough—the data might be removed from your file structure, but it’s still on your hard drive until it gets overwritten with more data. Unlink and uninstall all your programs. Many programs automatically sync with online cloud backups. This is a great boon to "}}
