{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_861229317#3_1956786279","relevance":3,"reason":"The page is dedicated to safely disposing of old computers and hardware and gives direct steps: back up data, wipe the hard drive, then donate, resell, or recycle the equipment. Although framed for company hardware, the disposal steps directly support the broader individual electronic-device disposal need.","learned":"Safe computer disposal steps include backing up data, securely wiping the hard drive, uninstalling/unlinking programs as needed, and then donating, reselling, or recycling the device."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3604","reason":"The current query is still producing dedicated disposal guidance with concrete data-wiping and reuse/recycling steps; continue to retrieve more grade-3 evidence."}}
